    <div class="about-text">
      <p>I'm a computer science student at Ontario Tech University specializing in embedded systems and software testing. Currently working as a Software/Systems Engineer Intern at the Rivian and Volkswagen joint venture, where I build tools that bridge requirements and firmware testing.</p>
      
      <p>At Ontario Tech Racing, I lead the embedded systems team building firmware for our Formula SAE electric car. The work spans everything from battery management to motor control, and I get to see it all come together on the track.</p>
      
      <p>I'm drawn to projects where software meets hardware—writing firmware that talks to sensors, building test infrastructure that catches bugs before they reach the track, and creating systems that need to work reliably in challenging conditions.</p>
      
      <p>When I'm not coding, you'll find me working on the FSAE car in the shop, debugging circuits on the bench, or learning about new embedded architectures.</p>
